<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a heap-buffer-overflow in the `handleattr` function in `src/core/specials.c`. The function receives a tuple `argv` and its length `argn`. The crash occurs because the code accesses `argv[0]` at line 311 without first checking if `argn` is greater than 0. When the fuzzer provides an empty tuple, `argn` is 0, and accessing `argv[0]` results in a read out of bounds.

The fix is to move the check `if (argn < 2)` at line 314 to before the access to `argv[0]` at line 311. This will ensure that the program doesn't try to access elements of an empty tuple.

```c
/* src/core/specials.c */
static JanetTable *handleattr(JanetCompiler *c, const char *kind, int32_t argn, const Janet *argv) {
if (argn < 2) { // Move this check up
janetc_error(c, janet_formatc("expected at least 2 arguments to %s", kind));
}
int32_t i;
JanetTable *tab = janet_table(2);
const char *binding_name = janet_type(argv[0]) == JANET_SYMBOL
? ((const char *)janet_unwrap_symbol(argv[0]))
: "<multiple bindings>";
/* ... */
}
```
</crash-analysis>

